--TEST--
A `Throwable`'s properties are `readonly`, so a write to a caught one's `message` is E0782 — `rule:classes/readonly-is-written-once`
--FILE--
<?nvs
try {
    throw new RuntimeError("a");
} catch (RuntimeError $e) {
    $e->message = "b";
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0782]: `Throwable::$message` is `readonly`, so only `Throwable`'s constructor writes it
  --> case.nvs:5:5
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
